Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Updated the classification of the command "bun x cowsay hello" from "general" to "cautious".
- Added new tests for package executors and package managers, marking their usage as "cautious".
- Introduced tests for decoding/obfuscating payloads piped to interpreters, marking them as "dangerous".
- Added tests for SSH authorized_keys writes and sudoers modifications, marking them as "dangerous".
- Included tests for shell RC file writes, git hook writes, and cron/systemd modifications, marking them as "cautious".
- Implemented tests for setuid/setgid and permission changes, marking them accordingly.
- Added tests for user/group account management and firewall rule modifications, marking them as "cautious" or "dangerous".
- Enhanced service management tests and mass process kill scenarios, marking them as "cautious" or "dangerous".
- Introduced tests for registry operations, network listeners, and HTTP servers, marking them as "cautious" or "dangerous".
- Added tests for package installs and remote file transfers, marking them as "cautious".
- Implemented tests for expanded protected root recursive deletes and .pem/.key file reads, marking them appropriately.
- Enhanced echo piped to interpreter tests and reverse shell pattern detections, marking them as "cautious" or "dangerous".
- Added tests for system destructive commands and tokenizer single quote backslash handling.
- Included tests for cmd /c payload integrity and git state change commands, marking them as "cautious".

